## Founding & History
Heriots Point Vineyard was established in 1996, with the first production of cool-climate Pinot Noir wines beginning in 2000. The vineyard is a small family farm.

## People
Evan Rolley is associated with Heriots Point, as he commented on the vineyard's participation in the 2023 Spring in the Vines event. The vineyard is described as a small family farm, with hand-tending of vines.

## Vineyard & Site
Heriots Point Vineyard is a three-hectare vineyard located on the western shores of the Huon River, nestled against the backdrop of the Wellington Ranges. The vines were first planted in 1996. The primary varietal planted is Pinot Noir. There is also a small, older planting of Chardonnay and Sylvaner vines. The farming approach involves hand-tending of vines.

## Cellar Door Experience
Heriots Point Vineyard's cellar door is located in a boat shed. It is open on Fridays, Saturdays, and Sundays from 11 am to 5 pm. The cellar door offers tastings of unique cellar-aged Pinots, with vintages from 2004 to 2013 mentioned. Group tastings are held at the boat shed, and private tastings can be booked for small groups. The cellar door pours a sparkling Pinot that is exclusively available on-site.

## Food & Hospitality
Heriots Point offers boutique accommodation in a peaceful vineyard cabin. The cabin features a king-sized bed, an ensuite shower and toilet, and a separate kitchen-living space with facilities for cooked meals. It has views over the vines to the Huon River and Wellington Mountain Ranges. The cost for the cabin is $185 for the first night and $170 for subsequent nights. The fridge can be stocked by order or guests can self-stock it. The vineyard is also available for weddings. Additionally, visitors can book a Huon River cruise on the heritage wooden boat "LaDrone," which departs from Heriots Point, and combine it with a wine tasting in the boat shed cellar door.

## Awards & Recognition
Heriots Point Pinot vintages from 2004 and 2009 have been described as "highly regarded".

## Sustainability & Certifications
No reliable information found from public sources.

## Visiting Practical Info
The address for Heriots Point Vineyard and Boutique Accommodation is 3883 Huon Highway, Castle Forbes Bay, TAS 7116, Australia. It is approximately a 40-minute drive from Hobart. The phone number is 0418 553 874. Another phone number, 0456 865 899, is also listed for enquiries regarding tastings and accommodation. The website is heriotspoint.com. An email address provided is info@heriotspoint.com and heriotspoint@gmail.com. Heriots Point Vineyard also has a Facebook presence.

## Notable / Distinctive
Heriots Point Vineyard is distinctive for its tranquil Huon riverside gardens and a boat shed tasting room. It offers unique cellar-aged Pinots, with vintages from 2004 to 2013 available for tasting. The vineyard provides the option for Huon River cruising and wine tasting on the heritage wooden boat "LaDrone". Their Pinot Sparkling is exclusively available at the cellar door. The vineyard is nestled on the western shores of the Huon River with panoramic views of the Wellington Ranges.

